@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# 832's re-vendor protocol: reference tooling for AEF T-3737
+
+This is consumer-side tooling from 832-Workflow-designer (its T-1000 and T-1005), offered as **reviewed input, not drop-in code**, as agreed. Every tool here works on a *vendoring project's* `.agentic-framework/` plus its `.vendor-divergence.yaml`. Where it should live is your decision: `fw upgrade`, `lib/`, or a vendored hook.
+
+## The problem it solves
+
+A re-vendor is one undifferentiated overwrite, so "upstream changed this" and "our local fix was lost" look the same. 832 lost local fixes this way at three successive upgrades. At 1.7.740 its divergence check, measured against a baseline that had not moved since v1.6.763, reported **1599 "unrecorded" paths**. Almost all of them were upstream changes, and the few real losses were buried among them.
+
+## The protocol
+
+1. **Pristine commit.** Commit the upgrade exactly as `fw upgrade` wrote it, alone (`.agentic-framework/` paths only, with VERSION changed).
+2. **Advance the baseline.** Point `baseline_commit` in `.vendor-divergence.yaml` at that commit. From then on, every *declared* local fix the upgrade overwrote shows as **STALE**, by name, with its task and reason. Real upstream changes stop showing as "unrecorded".
+3. **Work the list.** `tools/_t1000-revendor-worklist.py` lists each STALE fix with the diff from the old baseline to the pre-upgrade HEAD. Each one is re-applied, reclassified as superseded (upstream has it, proven by its probe), or dropped with a reason.
+4. **Done when `tools/_t517-vendor-divergence.py` is clean:** 0 stale, 0 unrecorded.
+
+**Gates** (`tools/_t1000-revendor-gate.sh`, installed into `.git/hooks/pre-commit` by `tools/_t1000-install-hook.sh`, because the framework hook has no project extension point):
+- **G1:** a commit that changes `.agentic-framework/VERSION` may contain only vendored paths.
+- **G2:** after a pristine commit, every commit is refused except the one that advances the baseline to it.
+- **G4:** a commit that changes a vendored path must have that path declared in `.vendor-divergence.yaml`. This is the declare-on-change rule.
+
+## Measured on one full cycle (1.7.740, 2026-10-02 to 2026-10-04)
+
+- **After the baseline advance:** 1599 → **0 unrecorded** and **51 STALE**, each named with its task. Before the protocol, the same tree reported 11 STALE and could not attribute the rest.
+- **After working the list:** 0 stale. Of 51 local fixes, some were re-applied, some were superseded upstream (each proven by its probe on the pristine tree), and some moved out of vendored files into project-owned code (`tools/project-audit.sh`), out of a re-vendor's reach.
+- **The gap the protocol cannot close by itself:** on 2026-10-04 832 found a fix (T-931's `fw task delegate` owner flip) that the upgrade had erased with **no trace**. It had been made before G4 existed, so it was never declared, and no test held it. The protocol only protects what is declared; G4 makes declaring mandatory from now on. For the backlog, 832 opened a one-off census (its T-1020). Your T-3737 ask stands: **list every vendored path whose pre-upgrade content differs from the baseline, declared or not, before overwriting.**
+
+## Running the test
+
+`bash contrib/832-revendor-protocol/tests/test_t1000_revendor_gate.sh` builds a scratch consumer repo, walks G1, G2 and G4, and passes 12/12. Every refusal leg has a matching allow leg, so a gate that refuses everything fails too.
diff --git a/contrib/832-revendor-protocol/tests/test_t1000_revendor_gate.sh b/contrib/832-revendor-protocol/tests/test_t1000_revendor_gate.sh
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d2cd6a38
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/832-revendor-protocol/tests/test_t1000_revendor_gate.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# T-1000: the re-vendor gate, walked through the protocol in a scratch git repo.
+# Each refusal leg has a pass leg beside it, so a gate that refuses everything fails too.
+# Run: bash tests/test_t1000_revendor_gate.sh   (exit 0 = all legs pass)
+set -u
+HERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
+GATE="$HERE/tools/_t1000-revendor-gate.sh"
+T=$(mktemp -d); trap 'rm -rf "$T"' EXIT
+pass=0; fail=0
+leg() { # leg <name> <want: ok|refused> <command...>
+    local name=$1 want=$2; shift 2
+    if "$@" >"$T/out" 2>&1; then got=ok; else got=refused; fi
+    if [ "$got" = "$want" ]; then pass=$((pass+1)); echo "PASS $name"; else fail=$((fail+1)); echo "FAIL $name (wanted $want, got $got)"; sed 's/^/     /' "$T/out" | head -8; fi
+}
+cd "$T" && git init -q r && cd r || exit 2
+git config user.email t@t; git config user.name t
+mkdir -p .agentic-framework/lib && echo 1.0.0 > .agentic-framework/VERSION && echo v1 > .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh && echo p > proj.txt
+printf 'baseline_commit: 0000000\npaths: []\n' > .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml
+git add -A && git commit -qm c0 --no-verify
+B0=$(git rev-parse HEAD); sed -i "s/0000000/$B0/" .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml; git commit -qam "baseline c0" --no-verify
+printf '#!/bin/bash\nbash "%s" || exit 1\n' "$GATE" > .git/hooks/pre-commit && chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit
+
+echo p2 >> proj.txt; git add proj.txt
+leg "1 ordinary project commit, no upgrade: allowed" ok git commit -qm ordinary
+
+echo 1.1.0 > .agentic-framework/VERSION; echo v2 > .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh; echo p3 >> proj.txt; git add -A
+leg "2 G1: upgrade commit mixed with a project file: refused" refused git commit -qm mixed
+git restore --staged proj.txt
+leg "3 G1: pristine upgrade commit (vendored paths only): allowed" ok git commit -qm pristine
+PRISTINE=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
+
+git add proj.txt
+leg "4 G2: ordinary commit right after the pristine commit: refused" refused git commit -qm too-early
+git restore --staged proj.txt
+sed -i "s/^baseline_commit: .*/baseline_commit: 1234567/" .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml; git add .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml
+leg "5 G2: baseline moved, but not to the pristine commit: refused" refused git commit -qm wrong-base
+sed -i "s/^baseline_commit: .*/baseline_commit: $PRISTINE/" .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml; git add .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml
+leg "6 G2: baseline advanced to the pristine commit: allowed" ok git commit -qm advance
+
+echo p5 >> proj.txt; git add proj.txt
+leg "7 after the advance, ordinary commits flow again: allowed" ok git commit -qm after
+
+echo local-fix >> .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh; git add .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh
+leg "9 G4: a local fix to an UNDECLARED vendored path: refused" refused git commit -qm undeclared
+printf '  - path: .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh\n    kind: content\n    task: T-X\n    upstream: fix\n    reason: test\n' >> .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml
+sed -i 's/^paths: \[\]$/entries:/' .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml
+git add .agentic-framework/.vendor-divergence.yaml .agentic-framework/lib/a.sh
+leg "10 G4: the same fix with its declaration staged: allowed" ok git commit -qm declared
+echo new > .agentic-framework/lib/b.sh; git add .agentic-framework/lib/b.sh
+leg "11 G4: an undeclared local ADDITION: refused" refused git commit -qm added-undeclared
+git restore --staged .agentic-framework/lib/b.sh; rm -f .agentic-framework/lib/b.sh
+
+echo 1.2.0 > .agentic-framework/VERSION; echo p4 >> proj.txt; git add -A
+leg "8 override is honoured and logged" ok env REVENDOR_GATE_OVERRIDE="test reason" git commit -qm overridden
+leg "8b the override was logged" ok grep -q "test reason" .context/working/revendor-gate-overrides.log
+
+echo; echo "T-1000 revendor gate: $pass passed, $fail failed"
+[ "$fail" -eq 0 ]
